<title>RUSSIA: Russia to buy 4.5 mln T maize, soymeal - minister.</title>
<headline>Russia to buy 4.5 mln T maize, soymeal - minister.</headline>
<dateline>ST PETERSBURG, Russia 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia will buy some 4.5 million tonnes of maize and soymeal from the United States, Canada and Australia this year, Agriculture Minister Viktor Khlystun told an industry meeting in St Petersburg on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>&quot;We intend to import 4-4.5 million tonnes of maize and soymeal, not only in 1996 but probably also in the coming years,&quot; he said. &quot;Russia does not produce enough maize.&quot;</p>
<p>Khlystun had said in early August that Russia would import 3-4 million tonnes of grains, mostly maize and soymeal, as well as about 500,000 tonnes of wheat, this year.</p>
<p>The purchases would be mostly for the Far East regions.</p>
<p>Russia forecasts a net grain harvest of 75-77 million tonnes this year, above last year's drought-hit 63.4 million tonnes.</p>
<p>But some regions like the Far East will still experience shortfalls.</p>
<p>-- Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
